<title>SPAIN: SOCCER-LEADING SCORERS IN THE SPANISH FIRST DIVISION.</title>
<headline>SOCCER-LEADING SCORERS IN THE SPANISH FIRST DIVISION.</headline>
<dateline>MADRID 1996-11-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Leading scorers in the Spanish</p>
<p>first division after games played on Sunday.</p>
<p>12 -  Ronaldo (Barcelona)</p>
<p>8  -  Davor Suker (Real Madrid)</p>
<p>7  -  Guilherme (Rayo Vallecano)</p>
<p>6  -  Jose Ziganda (Athletic Bilbao) Julen Guerrero (Athletic</p>
<p>Bilbao), Oli Alvarez (Oviedo), Gustavo Poyet (Zaragoza),</p>
<p>Juan Eduardo Esnaider (Atletico Madrid), Predrag Mijatovic</p>
<p>(Real Madrid)</p>
<p>5  -  Alfonso Perez (Real Betis), Rivaldo (Deportivo Coruna),</p>
<p>Alen Peternac (Valladolid), Raul Gonzalez (Real Madrid),</p>
<p>Fernando Correa (Racing Santander)</p>
</text>
